Compass: right-click a rock face to measure joints, Shift + E to measure the slope, E to write the reading into the field notebook@n@nMarkland planar sliding: a joint pole outside the friction circle, on the same side as the slope pole, and flatter than the slope (its great circle inside the slope's great circle) → sliding is possible=羅盤：右鍵岩面量節理、Shift＋E 量坡面、E 記進野帳本@n@nMarkland 平面滑動：節理極點在摩擦圓外、跟坡面極點同一側，而且比坡面緩（大圓在坡面大圓裡面）→ 可能滑動
E: write into the field notebook=E：記進野帳本
Geological compass@nRight-click a rock face to measure joints; Shift + E measures the slope; E writes it into the field notebook=地質羅盤@n右鍵岩面量節理；Shift＋E 量坡面；E 記進野帳本
You need a field notebook (the readings are kept in it)=需要野帳本（量測記在野帳本上）
